{number: 168}
{title: Lord, I Want to Be a Christian}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Lord, I want to be a Christian
In my [G7] heart, in my [C] heart.
Lord, I want to be a [F] Christian in my [C] heart.
In my [F] heart, in my [C] heart,
Lord, I want to be a [G7] Christian in my [C] heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Lord, I want to be more loving
In my [G7] heart, in my [C] heart.
Lord, I want to be more [F] loving in my [C] heart.
In my [F] heart, in my [C] heart,
Lord, I want to be more [G7] loving in my [C] heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Lord, I want to be more holy
In my [G7] heart, in my [C] heart.
Lord, I want to be more [F] holy in my [C] heart.
In my [F] heart, in my [C] heart,
Lord, I want to be more [G7] holy in my [C] heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Lord, I want to be like Jesus
In my [G7] heart, in my [C] heart.
Lord, I want to be like [F] Jesus in my [C] heart.
In my [F] heart, in my [C] heart,
Lord, I want to be like [G7] Jesus in my [C] heart.
{end_of_verse}
